  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{叱|しか}る (scold X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing action. {叱|しか}っている = 'is scolding.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{子供|こども}→子供：00554_kodomo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{叱|しか}る (scold a child)\n- {叱|しか}られる (be scolded—passive, very common)\n- ⟦{厳|きび}しく→厳しい：01125_kibishii⟧{叱|しか}る (scold harshly)\n- ⟦{愛情|あいじょう}→愛情：01673_aijou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{込|こ}めて{叱|しか}る (scold with love)\n\nCONTRAST WITH ⟦{怒|おこ}る→怒る：00876_okoru⟧:\n- {叱|しか}る: to scold (corrective, educational purpose)\n- ⟦{怒|おこ}る→怒る：00876_okoru⟧: to get angry (emotional reaction)\n\nIn theory, {叱|しか}る is done for the other person's benefit, while {怒|おこ}る is simply expressing anger. In practice, these often overlap.\n\nREGISTER: Neutral.",
